# Bergdb item 001, C-CUT (WP R7): a cut that CutOK's part 2 does not allow
# because of a stale reference. T(1) gives leaf 9 a new value; T(2) writes 9,
# 7, 5 and 3, but Java's version of 5 names 7's version of R(0), not that of
# R(2), which the model would name (so C-S fails for the references too). T(4)
# moves the first available time to 1 and decides a cut at 1; the startup pos
# is 3 then, so Rule R does not redirect the pointer. Expected: C-CUT fails
# with CUT-stale: a lookup at 1 reads 5's latest version, which leads to 7's
# version of R(0), before the cut.
TRACE 2
CONFIG stale
TX 0
NEW 0 9 I
NEW 3 8 I
NEW 5 3 I
NEW 7 2 I
NEW 9 1 I
ADD 0 0 T 3
ADD 3 0 R 5
ADD 5 0 K 10 7
ADD 7 0 K 1 9
REC 0 0 0 field 3
VER 3 I
H 0 R 5
F 5 0
VER 5 I
H 0 K 10 7
F 7 0
VER 7 I
H 0 K 1 9
F 9 0
VER 9 I
DIRTY
END 0
TX 1
NEW 11 0 D
ADD 11 1 V 5
ADD 9 1 K 2 11
REC 1 0 0 field 3
VER 11 D
H 1 V 5
GD 3 5 7 9
DIRTY 3 1 5 1 7 1 9 1
END 1
TX 2
REC 2 1 2 field 3
VER 9 I
H 1 K 2 11
F 11 1
VER 7 I
H 0 K 1 9
F 9 2
VER 5 I
H 0 K 10 7
F 7 0
VER 3 I
H 0 R 5
F 5 2
GD
DIRTY
END 2
TX 3
REC 3 2 2 field 3
GD
DIRTY
END 3
TX 4
REC 4 3 2 field 3
GD
DIRTY
FA 1
CUT 1 1
END 4
DONE 4
